# Build output
build/
# Catches CLion's cmake-build-debug/ + cmake-build-release/ + any other
# cmake-build-<name>/ flavor a contributor might generate locally.
cmake-build-*/
out/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeUserPresets.json
cmake_install.cmake
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
# Anchored to the repo root so a future source dir or asset named
# `hxediter` (e.g. src/hxediter/) isn't silently swallowed. Only the
# in-tree-build binary at ./hxediter is the intended target — actual
# release builds land in build/ and are already covered above.
/hxediter
/hxsort
# Mach-O debug symbol bundles (clang emits these next to the binary in
# some build configurations) and the .dmg release artifact (already
# covered by build/, kept here defensively in case someone runs cpack
# elsewhere).
*.dSYM/
*.dmg

# IDE / editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.claude/

# Dear ImGui runtime state
imgui.ini

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
# Apple metadata stored as separate ._* files on non-HFS filesystems
# (USB sticks, network shares) — would otherwise pollute every dir.
._*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Secrets / signing — never commit credentials or signing material.
# Especially load-bearing for release.sh's Phase 6 (Developer ID +
# notarization): *.p12 is the exported Developer ID Application cert
# including its private key, and *.p8 is the App Store Connect API key
# consumed by `xcrun notarytool` — either one alone is enough for an
# attacker to ship a signed, notarized build under your identity.
*.p12
*.p8
*.pem
*.key
*.cer
*.crt
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
.env
.env.*
.netrc
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# Per-release artifacts from the release workflow
SHA256SUMS.txt
*.log
